- Session 8 — UX + the owner's 3 questions answered concretely (multi-user / uninstall / auto-update):
- Session 8 — UX + the owner's 3 questions answered concretely (multi-user / uninstall / auto-update):
  • MULTI-USER (it already is — made it obvious + robust): the app is a STATIC CLIENT-SIDE reader. Each visitor
    connects their OWN local save in their OWN browser via the File System Access API — nothing uploaded, no account,
    no shared backend → anyone can use it independently and no one can see anyone else's data. Hosting (Pages/Vercel)
    only decides where the page lives; end users never "log in." Added a "👥 No account, no sign-in — anyone can open
    it and connect their own save; your data never leaves your device" line to the connect screen. ROBUSTNESS: Disconnect
    now resets the loot tracking (lastUids + lootLog + clears persisted tbh_loot + logData) so switching to a DIFFERENT
    save on the same browser is a clean slate (was: diffed against the old save → false-flood the timeline). Normal page
    reloads don't disconnect, so the timeline still survives reloads of the SAME save. Verified headless (2→0, storage removed).
  • AUTO-UPDATE — now VISIBLE (it worked, but silently): main.js wires electron-updater events
    (update-available/download-progress/update-downloaded/error) → renderer; preload exposes onUpdate + restartToUpdate;
    a friendly bottom banner shows "Downloading update… N%" then "Update ready · vX — restart to apply" + a Restart button
    (quitAndInstall). autoInstallOnAppQuit=true also applies on next quit without a click. Web never fires these (the hosted
    page is always current on load). Verified the banner states headless (downloading/ready/dismiss). When we publish a new
    release, installed apps auto-download + offer restart.
  • UNINSTALL — confirmed + polished: NSIS oneClick:false already builds an uninstaller (builder-debug.yml shows
    WriteUninstaller + uninstaller.nsh) + an Add/Remove Programs entry. Added uninstallDisplayName "TBH HUD", desktop +
    Start-Menu shortcuts, runAfterFinish, deleteAppDataOnUninstall:false. Rebuilt the 1.0.2 installer (valid; new latest.yml).
  • README: added a 3-question FAQ (multi-user / uninstaller / auto-update) in plain language.
